    "description": "Application Developer for Remedy – an Apache Struts based web application used across all lines of businesses in the Investment Bank and by traders to mark credit risk, deployed on Weblogic 10.0. Remedy consists of two main components - WebMP is the website for creating, and marking risk data. CSQ is the website for reporting on the data stored in Remedy. There is also an XML interface for systems to access this data.\n\n-Duties include:\n•\tAdding functionality and enhancements to the Remedy Web Application by implementing code changes (Java code base/JSP),\n•\tWrite/enhance stand alone Java applications used to support Remedy\n•\tProviding or modifying stored procedures (Sybase database), and providing or modifying shell/perl scripts.\n•\tActing as release manager to provide application enhancements to the end users.\n-Large-scale projects include:\n•\tDeveloping a process to map bonds received from a daily feed to Remedy curves (Perl script/Java application).\n•\tModifying the linked point formula to allow for the use of both spread and factor values in the calculation of follower rates. This involved changes to the Java code base, the WebMP interface(JSP), and database.\n•\tDeveloping a bulk curve creation tool after the merger with  Bear Stearns (Java application)\n•\tDesigning an xml query to mark curves from the new source, TraderFuse. This involved the addition of new business logic to the Java code base.\n•\tCurrently assisting on migrating the Remedy application from a unix server to linux.\n•\tCurrently assisting on the rearchitecture project for Remedy – moving to a multi clustered environment for parallel processing of requests.\n-Work to maintain a stable environment to support increased volumes and business expansion by resolving application   \n issues and providing client support on a daily basis. Usually involving bug fixes to the business logic in Remedy (Java ).",
