  "about": "I have received a BA in Psychology from The University of Texas as well as an MS in Computer Science from The University of Houston with a 3.42 GPA. My previous positions have given me experience with Perl, SQL, and Java. I am also familiar with C and C++ from courses taken at UH.\nMy experience in Java comes from my current position as well as my position as an Intern at JPMorgan Chase. Both as an Intern and my current role I have written/enhanced stand alone Java applications such as a process that monitors the arrival of supplier feed files and a process to retrieve bond data from an outside vendor and update our internal database.\nThe majority of the work involved with my current position involves maintenance and enhancement of Remedy, a critical application used across all lines of business at JPMorgan Chase in the Investment Bank. Remedy is a consolidated system for capturing, storing and syndicating credit market data. Remedy consists of two main components - WebMP is the website for creating, and marking CDS (credit default swaps) curves and other credit related curves (market values across multiple horizons). CSQ is the website for reporting on the data stored in Remedy. There is also an XML interface for systems to access this data. Aside from WebMP, Remedy receives market data from other internal systems via XML, and Remedy receives external feeds of data from multiple vendors. Remedy is a struts based application built and deployed on Weblogic 10.0 server. Most of my assignments involve modification of the business logic (java code base) and occasionally the jsp pages. For example, enhancements to the logic for leader/follower relationships between curves, adding additional attributes to a curve, creating a new xml request for users to  retrieve a derived rating for an SPN (standard party number, a company), and bug fix for errors in the calculation of follower spread data based on their leader.",
